                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Mr. Hay directs Mr. Griscom to officially communicate to the minister for
                    foreign affairs and unofficially to the palace that the President relies upon
                    the Turkish Government promptly paying £20,000 indemnity for value of property
                    of American citizens destroyed in 1895. Promise of payment made in December,
                    1898, should be fulfilled without further postponement, and when irade is issued
                    to cable the Department.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
